here's a Java function to find and print all matches of a given regex inside a string:

```java
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class RegexMatcher {
  public static void findMatches(String input, String regex) {
    Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile(regex);
    Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(input);

    while (matcher.find()) {
      System.out.println("Match found: " + matcher.group());
    }
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    String input = "This is an example string with an address https://www.example.com.";
    String regex = "example\\.com";
    findMatches(input, regex);
  }
}
```

this function, `findMatches`, takes a string and a regex as inputs. it compiles the regex into a `Pattern` object and uses a `Matcher` object to find all matches within the string. for each match, it prints the matched substring. the `main` method tests this function with the provided input and regex, and the output will be:

```
Match found: example.com
